Subject: [PATCH] AGENTS.md: document the review material-input pinning rule

HUMAN-APPLIED PATCH — for the human to review and apply. AGENTS.md is on
the agent edit-deny list, and this change does not weaken any agent
permission restriction, so it is delivered as a patch rather than applied
by an agent (Plan 4, decision B.3).

Apply from the phys-research repository root:

    git apply --check ../AGENTS.md.review-input-pinning.patch   # dry run
    git apply      ../AGENTS.md.review-input-pinning.patch      # apply

It documents the behaviour implemented in commit 71d0dfe:
  - a review pins one digest per material input (one-hop neighbours in
    both directions, review records excluded: P-001, I-001, E-001 for H-001);
  - creation fails with an explicit diagnostic rather than silently
    skipping an unreadable or unparseable material input;
  - validate and status share one freshness rule, so a changed target or
    a changed material input is STALE in both;
  - a review with no input lines is LEGACY_UNPINNED (warning, exit 0),
    never "fully fresh".

Verified: `git apply --check` passes against AGENTS.md at commit 71d0dfe.

